description:
Slice of CQ-M07 (task-1a8f1d0e199046a289e94a5453d758b8, the final acceptance row): M07 DoD 7, the contracts and troubleshooting half. Filed by its planner architect-c33f294e on 2026-11-04. Docs only. It depends on CQ-M07t (task-527735ea; through it CQ-M07s and CQ-M07r), because the troubleshooting rows include the codes those rows add. It runs in parallel with CQ-M07v1 (task-63e6fb62), which owns CONFIGURATION, ARCHITECTURE, CERTIFICATION and the architect reference.

OBJECTIVE. Pay the doc debts the M07 slices deferred to this sweep, all from landed code.

DELIVERABLE
- docs/MCP_SERVER.md:
  - a section for moe.get_execution_readiness and its /ws twin GET_EXECUTION_READINESS -> EXECUTION_READINESS (CQ-M07d, tools/getExecutionReadiness.ts): payload {profile, ready, missingCapabilities, evaluatedAt}, refresh and its rate limit, non-blocking, read-only;
  - a section for moe.get_seat_liveness (CQ-M07g0): {workerId, registered, status, openAttempts}, wrapper-only. A seat is gone only when (!registered || status === 'DEAD') && openAttempts === 0;
  - executionRoute 'vm' on claim_next_task and wait_for_task (CQ-M07q), if it is not documented yet;
  - the serverCapabilities verifiedLocal value. The doc shows false near lines 3210/3215; it has been true since CQ-M07d2;
  - the strict-consumer DONE/ARCHIVED sentences near lines 1242, 1249, 1274, 1464, 1508 and 1996 (task-7aa6be67's residuals): a verified-local consumer needs retained verified delivery, and a missing prerequisite never satisfies it;
  - the two advisory points in comment-c16cb64b on the final row. In get_context's Execution policy paragraph, the "non-strict effectiveProfile" sentence holds only when the TASK snapshot is not verified-local. In Strict completion (CQ-F08), "completes as legacy after the rollback" also covers a rollback to observe.
- docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:
  - one row per code the wrappers print on the VM route: the MOE_VERIFIED_LOCAL_*, MOE_SEAT_* and MOE_VM_* families, and the check-gate and receipt lines CQ-M07r/s/t add;
  - one row per readiness id in READINESS_IDS (delivery/executionReadiness.ts) with its operator action. For example: certification-report-missing means run certify; certification-report-mismatch means re-certify after an upgrade; protected-host-control-plane means run the plugin-installed daemon; revision-bound-local-delivery means set deliveryPolicy local-branch.

NOT IN SCOPE: CONFIGURATION, ARCHITECTURE, CERTIFICATION and docs/roles (CQ-M07v1); any code; the cq-m06 README.

VERIFICATION: `npm run lint`, then the daemon suite (docs guard tests, including the one that needs a section per registered tool) in a git-archive snapshot of HEAD with this task's docs overlaid: npm ci, then `npm test` under env -i with Linux node 24.
